## Dirichlet Root Noise (train.json::mcts.selfplay ONLY)

| Field | Purpose | Typical values |
|-------|---------|---------------|
| dirichlet_alpha | Noise concentration. Lower = more uniform, higher = more peaked. | 0.167 (quoridor), 0.33 (splendor), 1.0-1.2 (short games) |
| dirichlet_epsilon | Noise weight (0=no noise, 1=all noise). | 0.25 (standard) |
| dirichlet_on_first_n_plies | -1 = whole game. | -1 for most; explicit value to restrict noise to opening |

### alpha by action space
- Rule of thumb for fixed `dirichlet_alpha`: `alpha ~ 10 / action_space_size` (tictactoe `1.0`, loveletter `1.0`, coup `0.5-1.2`, quoridor `0.17`).
- **Preferred for variable or wide branching (`N >= 20`)**: set `dirichlet_alpha: 0.0`, `dirichlet_total_alpha: 10.83`, and `dirichlet_shaped: true` (KataGo adaptive + log-prior shaped concentration: 50% uniform `1/N` + 50% excess log-prior capped at `max(0.01, 1/N)`). See `training-exploration` and `training-overconfidence`.

